    "result_text": "All 273 tests pass, including the new `Cp09Tests`, with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented sequential membership numbers for newly created owners (`POST /api/owners`), returned in the owner response as the integer field `membershipNumber`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `membershipNumber` property (readOnly `integer`/`int32`) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct maps it automatically.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `membershipNumber` column with getter/setter. Persisting it means the value is stable and returned by the `GET /api/owners/{id}` read the acceptance test uses.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 Added the nullable `membership_number` column to the `owners` table.\n\n4. **`function/owner/AssignMembershipNumber.java`** (new) \u2014 Reads the built `Owner`, sets `membershipNumber = ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1` (one more than the current owner count).\n\n5. **`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 Wired the new `assignMembershipNumber` step into the pipeline after the uniqueness checks and before `save` (under the write `transaction` governance).\n\nThe number is computed before the new owner is saved, so it equals one more than the pre-existing count; the `Cp09Tests` invariant (two consecutive creations differ by exactly one) holds because the query autoflushes the prior insert within the transaction.",
